{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 22, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur awoke to the smell of pine and damp earth. Sunlight dappled through leaves he'd never seen before, vibrant greens and golds unlike anything in his apartment. He sat up, a strange disorientation washing over him. His hands felt…different. Stronger. He glanced down and saw calloused palms, not the smooth skin he remembered. A flicker of something – a glint of metal – caught his eye. He reached for it, his fingers brushing against a worn leather bracer adorned with a stylized wolf’s head. Panic tightened his chest. He tried to sit up straighter, and his muscles responded with a surprising surge of power. He looked around, noticing the details: the rough-hewn wooden walls of a small cabin, the intricately carved symbols on the door, the faint echo of birdsong that seemed almost…programmed. This wasn’t his life. This wasn’t real.\n\n***\n\nA wave of nausea hit him as he realized the impossible. The texture of the wood, the way the sunlight filtered, the very air itself – it all felt meticulously crafted, designed. He tested his reflexes, dodging a low-hanging branch that seemed to appear out of nowhere. His movements were faster, more precise than he’d ever been. He felt a surge of adrenaline, a thrill of power mixed with utter terror. A voice, clear and resonant, echoed in his mind, not spoken aloud, but directly implanted. \"Welcome, Adventurer. The world awaits.\" Arthur scrambled to his feet, the bracer feeling warm against his skin. He was no longer Arthur Penhaligon, accountant. He was something…else. He was a character in a game, and the game had just begun.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.7662928104400635}, {"token": "▁awoke", "logprob": -0.4878727197647095}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.0028092702850699425}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.00702104065567255}, {"token": "▁smell", "logprob": -1.7410707473754883}, {"toke